    {"q":"What is real-world evidence (RWE) in healthcare?","opts":["Lab experiments","Clinical evidence derived from real-world data outside traditional clinical trials","Hospital reviews","Patient testimonials"],"correct":1,"explain":"RWE uses data from EHRs, claims, registries, and wearables to complement traditional clinical trial evidence.","difficulty":"hard"},
    {"q":"What is the challenge of missing data in clinical datasets?","opts":["It's never a problem","Missing data can introduce bias and reduce statistical power if not handled properly","It means the study is invalid","It only affects small studies"],"correct":1,"explain":"Missing data mechanisms (MCAR, MAR, MNAR) determine the appropriate imputation or analysis strategy.","difficulty":"hard"},
    {"q":"What is a Cox proportional hazards model?","opts":["A hospital safety model","A regression model for analyzing the effect of variables on time-to-event outcomes","A billing system","A patient scheduling tool"],"correct":1,"explain":"Cox regression estimates hazard ratios, showing how covariates affect the rate of an event occurring.","difficulty":"hard"},
    {"q":"What is the role of synthetic data in health research?","opts":["Replacing all real data","Generating artificial data that preserves statistical properties while protecting patient privacy","Creating fake patients","Simulating hospital operations"],"correct":1,"explain":"Synthetic data mimics real patient data distributions without containing actual PHI, enabling safe research.","difficulty":"hard"}
